# Lessons Learned

This room reinforced several important penetration testing concepts.

- Never overlook anonymous FTP access.
- Writable directories can quickly lead to remote code execution.
- Packet captures often contain valuable intelligence.
- Enumeration is the most important phase of an engagement.
- Small vulnerabilities become critical when chained together.
- Always inspect scheduled tasks and root-owned scripts during privilege escalation.

---

# Final Thoughts

Startup is an excellent beginner room because it demonstrates an end-to-end attack chain rather than focusing on a single vulnerability. It helped reinforce practical enumeration, reverse shells, packet analysis, credential discovery, and Linux privilege escalation in a realistic environment.

